Arrgghh!  "omega" just core-dumped on me again when I was on first level
getting ready to kill a goblin.  One of the problems with core dump
anyplace other than the city level is that your file is not saved.  Only on
city level does it go through the process of asking you about it.  Can the
author of this program please try doing it again...
BTW, it seems that the program has no need for a "header.h" file.  I've
compiled it without it and am having the above occasion core dump.  Very
annoying when the guards keep getting in the way.
	It would be nice if some Moria features could be added here, mainly
a mapping system so that we can have an idea of where we are on a
particular level and be able to get a hardcopy of the present map.  It sure
would help in this game.
	Also, can we get some real documentation, especially on how to use
"wizard" mode.  The normal instructions don't and shouldn't have this
information.

